    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XYC9n7jY4gV3tnop2oYDSv)_\n\n## Problem\n`C-x t s` reports `vulpea-ui-sidebar-toggle` as undefined. (Separate from #130, which fixed `C-x s t`.)\n\n## Cause\n`sp-vulpea-ui.el` declared `(use-package vulpea-ui ... :after vulpea)` and bound the key with a plain `global-set-key`. `vulpea` is loaded lazily (its own `:bind`), so the `:after` form never ran and `vulpea-ui` was never loaded; a plain `global-set-key` creates no autoload.\n\n## Fix\nDrop `:after vulpea` and bind `C-x t s` with `:bind` in the same `use-package`, which autoloads `vulpea-ui-sidebar-toggle` from `vulpea-ui`. `vulpea-ui` requires `vulpea` itself. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Verification\nNot run in Emacs (none in the sandbox); this is from reading the code. Please check `C-x t s` in a fresh Emacs. If it still says undefined, `M-: (locate-library \"vulpea-ui\")` shows whether Elpaca installed it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ad8QyaD8EpsqigU9Prgkef)_",
